.TH LATTICE 1
.SH NAME
lattice \- a turtle with width, curvature and layers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/lattice
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Lattice
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Lattice.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The pen is a segment, not a point: every micro-step draws a line across
the turtle's width perpendicular to its heading, so a stroke is a ribbon
with its own edge colour, and the number of micro-steps is chosen from
the width and the speed together, which keeps a fat fast stroke from
coming out as dashes.
.PP
The curvature comes from a table of thirty-five entries, and the table is
the interesting part: two pi over 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 12, 15, 18,
20, 24, 30, 36, 40 and their negatives, with zero in the middle.  Every
entry closes a circle in a whole number of steps, so a curve always comes
back to where it started.
.PP
The z is a layer, kept in the depth buffer, so a stroke on a higher layer
covers lower ones however they are drawn.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B space
Step the turtle
.TP
.B "left / right"
Turn the curvature table
.TP
.B "up / down"
Accelerate, brake
.TP
.B + / -
Wider, narrower
.TP
.B 0-9
Layer
.TP
.B c
Colour, middle then edge
.TP
.B e
Rounded ends on or off
.TP
.B LMB
Move the turtle; RMB aims it
.TP
.B Enter
Clear
.TP
.B q
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/lattice.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
